+[markdown cell tabs19_q4_heading]
+### Apply the Delivery Rules
+
+```{index} Practice
+```
+
+
+[markdown cell tabs19_q4_task]
+Prepare one delivery quote. The recognized services are express `E` at 8, standard `S` at 3, and pickup `P` at zero. Standard delivery is free when `orderTotal >= 50m`; the waiver does not apply to express. An unknown code must print `Unknown service`.
+
+Complete the marked area using the selection forms taught in this reading. Use top-level statements; no loop or method is required. The starter compiles and prints `Not implemented` until you supply the rule.
+
+| Service | Order total | Required report |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| E | 25.00 | `Service E: 8` |
+| S | 49.99 | `Service S: 3` |
+| S | 50.00 | `Service S: 0` |
+| P | 25.00 | `Service P: 0` |
+| X | 50.00 | `Unknown service` |
+
+Change the two supplied input values and run each row separately.
+
+```{dropdown} Hint
+Recognize the service first. Apply the threshold waiver only to standard delivery. Keep recognition separate from the numeric charge so that pickup and invalid input cannot be confused.
+```
+
+
+[code cell tabs19_quote_starter]
+// Exercise: apply delivery rules
+// exercise-id: cscs-decision-practice-delivery-tabs
+using System;
+string service = "S";
+decimal orderTotal = 50m;
+string report = "Not implemented";
+// Your code starts here.
+// TODO: recognize the service, apply the standard-delivery waiver, and set report.
+// Your code ends here.
+Console.WriteLine(report);
+
+
+[code cell tabs19_quote_solution]
+// Solution: apply delivery rules
+using System;
+string service = "S";
+decimal orderTotal = 50m;
+string report = "Not implemented";
+int charge = 0;
+bool recognized = true;
+switch (service)
+{
+    case "E": charge = 8; break;
+    case "S": charge = 3; break;
+    case "P": charge = 0; break;
+    default: recognized = false; break;
+}
+if (recognized && service == "S" && orderTotal >= 50m) charge = 0;
+if (recognized) report = $"Service {service}: {charge}";
+else report = "Unknown service";
+Console.WriteLine(report);
+
+
+[markdown cell tabs19_q4_feedback]
+The initial S/50 input prints `Service S: 0`. The code first answers “was the service recognized?” and then applies the waiver, so X/50 is still rejected. Test just below and exactly at 50 to check the inclusive boundary; test E/50 as well to ensure a standard-only policy has not spread to every service.
 
 
